----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SURFACE DESIGN (parity with the web source)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <Slider> is a controlled single-thumb `<input type=range>` primitive: required `label`
(visible + a11y name), optional `formatValue` readout (`aria-valuetext`), `showLabel` + `disabled`
flags, `min`/`max`/`step`, `onChange`. Its only "data source" is React `useId` (label↔input id
association) — SwiftUI associates a control with its label automatically, so no explicit id is
modelled. Files (7 swift + 1 strings), collision-free names (TSSlider + SwiftUI.Slider already exist):
  Slider.swift          — SliderSurface host (state machine) + surfaceSlug="Slider"      (101 loc)
  Slider.Model.swift    — SliderStrings(i18n S10), SliderTelemetry+OSLog(S11), SliderValueFormat,
                          SliderConfig, SliderConnection, SliderInput, SliderSource+SliderModel(S8) (355)
  Slider.Source.swift   — InMemorySliderSource (preview/test seam)                         (56)
  Slider.Adapter.swift  — SliderProjection.resolve -> SliderResolved (error→loading→empty→ready) (98)
  Slider.Views.swift    — SliderControl (primitive parity) + loading/error/empty chrome +
                          freshness chip + connectivity banner (self-contained)            (266)
  Slider.Previews.swift — #if DEBUG previews per state + format/disabled/no-label variants  (144)
  Slider.Tests.swift    — XCTest: projection / formatter / snap / model wiring / a11y       (283)
  Slider.strings        — i18n catalog (P4 leaf chrome + demo labels)
Every state renders: loading (skeleton), empty (unusable bounds), error (retry), ready
(interactive control), + the live/stale/offline freshness axis (chip + banner + one-shot stale
auto-refresh). view.opened telemetry emitted once on first presentation (slug "Slider").
Bound through SliderSource (P1/S8); no view-side I/O. All chrome strings via SliderStrings (P1/S10).
a11y: SwiftUI Slider carries label + aria-valuetext-equivalent accessibilityValue + native
adjustable action; visible label row hidden from VO to avoid duplication; Dynamic Type via tokens;
Reduce-Motion respected (TSFadeIn + skeleton pulse).

